 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"PPC Landing Page Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a PPC landing page?\", \"a\": \"A PPC landing page is the page a visitor reaches after clicking a paid ad, written for that ad alone. It carries one offer and a headline that echoes the ad, with no navigation leading elsewhere.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you build a landing page for paid ads?\", \"a\": \"Start with one ad group and the offer its ads promise, then write the page around that promise. With Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>, you describe the ad group, the offer, and the form in a prompt, and Emergent builds the page and the lead table behind it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is landing page experience?\", \"a\": \"Landing page experience is the Google Ads rating of how relevant and useful a page is to the people who click an ad. It feeds Quality Score alongside expected clickthrough rate and ad relevance, and it is judged against other advertisers showing for the same search.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you design a good pay per click landing page?\", \"a\": \"Design it to agree with the ad. A good pay per click landing page opens on the words the visitor searched and quotes the price the ad quoted. It then asks for a single action, a short form or a call, with nothing else competing for the click.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are dynamic landing pages for PPC?\", \"a\": \"They are pages that change part of their copy to suit the click. A parameter in the ad's link, for example the keyword or the service, decides which headline and image appear. One page can then serve many ad groups. Emergent builds that logic from a plain description of the values and the headlines.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the best practices for a PPC landing page?\", \"a\": \"Relevance comes first in Google Ads landing page best practices: the page should deliver what the ad promised. The same guidance stresses pages that are easy to use on a phone and quick to load. Guides written for the older AdWords landing page give the same advice.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should PPC landing pages include?\", \"a\": \"A headline that answers the search, the offer with its price, and one way to respond. Ask only for the details the offer needs: a repair quote may need a zip code, while a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/webinar-landing-page'>webinar landing page</a> needs little more than a name and an email.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you track leads from paid landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Pass the keyword and the campaign into the page through the final URL, and store both with every form entry. Count the conversion when the visitor reaches the thank you page after submitting. Pages built with Emergent keep those leads in a database you own, with the keyword in its own column.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a below average landing page experience?\", \"a\": \"It is the lowest of the three ratings Google Ads gives a landing page, under average and above average. It means visitors find less of what the ad led them to expect than on competing pages. Rewriting the headline to match the keyword is the usual first fix.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should you create a separate PPC landing page for each ad group?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when the ad groups sell different things. A dentist bidding on implants and on teeth whitening needs two pages with different offers. Ad groups that differ only in wording can share one page whose headline changes with a value in the URL.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}